+## Data from PDF: additive column recovery
+
+After legacy extraction, the runner can retain a nearby unlabelled left-column block
+under `data.fields.unlabeledAfterVisitNo`, `unlabeledAfterVisitNoPage`, and
+`unlabeledAfterVisitNoLine1` (and subsequent numbered lines). Populated right-side
+labels and mixed rows are supported when retained line text and positions provide
+sufficient evidence. Existing keys and values, including legacy `unlabeledAfter...`
+blocks, are preserved. These keys describe layout, not the semantic identity of a
+person or address; downstream mappings must be reviewed for each layout.
+The actual preceding label determines the key: Visit No gives `unlabeledAfterVisitNo`,
+and ACC gives `unlabeledAfterAcc`, including when the ACC field is populated.
+An occupied field family (even a blank or partial one) is preserved as a whole;
+a distinct new block uses `unlabeledAfterAccBlock2` and its own Page/Line keys,
+incrementing the block suffix until free. Repeated recovery does not duplicate blocks.
+
+The recovery uses line text/x/y and existing fields. It requires at least two aligned
+rows close below a labelled row in the right column. Unknown labels, large gaps, and
+alignment changes stop the pass. It cannot resolve all column ambiguities in flattened
+line text. The JSON replay harness in `DataFromPdfActivities.Replay` exercises the exact
+recovery source without original PDFs. Such replays do not verify PDF ingestion,
+word grouping, segment splitting, or legacy extraction. Clinical continuation limits
+are unchanged. The runner architecture, installers, and dependencies are unchanged.
